With the **same denominator**, the fraction with the larger numerator is larger: $\tfrac{3}{5} > \tfrac{2}{5}$.
[tikz]
% mathsmap-diagram-colours {"version":1,"kind":"geometry","base":[],"semantic":[{"name":"fractionBlue","hex":"D4E8FF","reason":"Shaded numerator area or marked numerator objects"},{"name":"fractionOrange","hex":"FCE8D5","reason":"Second model numerator area or marked objects"}],"reference":"Existing fraction partitions/marked regions retained; standard light fills represent shaded fractional parts; ordinary marks black"}
\definecolor{fractionBlue}{HTML}{D4E8FF}
\definecolor{fractionOrange}{HTML}{FCE8D5}
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large},x=0.65cm,y=0.65cm]
\foreach \i in {0,...,2} {\fill[fractionBlue] (\i,1.8) rectangle (\i+1,2.8);}
\draw (0,1.8) rectangle (5,2.8);
\foreach \i in {1,...,4} {\draw (\i,1.8)--(\i,2.8);}
\node[right] at (5.3,2.3) {$\frac35$};
\foreach \i in {0,...,1} {\fill[fractionOrange] (\i,0) rectangle (\i+1,1);}
\draw (0,0) rectangle (5,1);
\foreach \i in {1,...,4} {\draw (\i,0)--(\i,1);}
\node[right] at (5.3,0.5) {$\frac25$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

For equal-sized wholes, thirds are larger than sixths: $\frac{1}{3}=\frac{2}{6}>\frac{1}{6}$.
[tikz]
% mathsmap-diagram-colours {"version":1,"kind":"geometry","base":[],"semantic":[{"name":"fractionBlue","hex":"D4E8FF","reason":"Shaded numerator area or marked numerator objects"},{"name":"fractionOrange","hex":"FCE8D5","reason":"Second model numerator area or marked objects"}],"reference":"Source-adapted related thirds/sixths on equal wholes; standard light fills mark fractional areas; ordinary outlines/labels black"}
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.8cm,y=0.7cm]
\definecolor{fractionBlue}{HTML}{D4E8FF}
\definecolor{fractionOrange}{HTML}{FCE8D5}
\fill[fractionBlue] (0,1.7) rectangle (2,2.7);
\draw[black] (0,1.7) rectangle (6,2.7);
\foreach \i in {2,4} {\draw[black] (\i,1.7)--(\i,2.7);}
\node[right,text=black] at (6.2,2.2) {$\frac13$};
\fill[fractionOrange] (0,0) rectangle (1,1);
\draw[black] (0,0) rectangle (6,1);
\foreach \i in {1,...,5} {\draw[black] (\i,0)--(\i,1);}
\node[right,text=black] at (6.2,0.5) {$\frac16$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

